Largest Zigzag Sequence
Solved
Difficulty: EasyAccuracy: 50.0%Submissions: 18K+Points: 2Average Time: 20m
Given a square matrix mat[][] of size n × n. A zigzag sequence starts from the top and ends at the bottom. Two consecutive elements of sequence cannot belong to the same column.

Return the maximum sum of such a zigzag sequence.







  class Solution {
  public:
    int zigzagSequence(vector<vector<int>>& mat) {
        //code here
        int n=mat.size();
        vector<vector<long long>>dp(n,vector<long long>(n,0));
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++) dp[0][i]=mat[0][i];
        
        long long ans=0;
        for(int i=1;i<n;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<n;j++){
                 
                 for(int k=0;k<n;k++){
                     if(k!=j){
                         dp[i][j]=max(dp[i][j], (long long)mat[i][j] + dp[i-1][k]);
                     }
                 }
            }
        }
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
             ans=max(ans,dp[n-1][i]);
        }
        return ans;
        
    }
};
